Terminologies
-------------

This repository contains no UMLS Metathesaurus files, no value-set expansions and no vocabulary tables. The code
downloads terminology content at run time with each user's own UMLS license. The analyses reported in the study used:

- value-set expansions from the Value Set Authority Center (VSAC) of the U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM), as
  bundled in CMS's measure packages (VSAC manifest of 17 November 2025) or downloaded from VSAC;
- RxNorm, full monthly release of 5 October 2026, from NLM.

This content was obtained from NLM under the UMLS Metathesaurus License (2026AA). NLM is the source of this content.
Neither NLM nor the organizations whose vocabularies are included in the UMLS have endorsed this software.

Some material in the UMLS Metathesaurus is from copyrighted sources of the respective copyright holders. Users of the
UMLS Metathesaurus are solely responsible for compliance with any copyright, patent or trademark restrictions and are
referred to the copyright, patent or trademark notices appearing in the original sources, all of which are hereby
incorporated by reference.

Vocabularies used, and what of each appears in this repository (a portion only in every case):

- RxNorm (NLM): one concept identifier (253182) in a unit test, one drug name in a code comment, and ingredient and
  brand words in search patterns.
- SNOMED CT, US Edition (version of 1 September 2024, as carried in CMS's value-set expansions): five concept
  identifiers and one description, in the mapping and readiness-check code.
- LOINC (Regenstrief Institute): one code (2345-7) in a unit test.
- ICD-10-CM and ICD-9-CM: code system identifiers only; no codes.

